# Crystal Imperium play test: the stat editor with Minimal Grinding on (the default, DECISIONS.md
# D3 and D34). Every Pokemon battles at 31 IVs and 0 EVs, so as in Emerald Imperium the EVs are
# locked (LEFT/RIGHT stay on the IVs) and the IVs only set Hidden Power's type: an HP IV of 30
# with the rest at 31 makes it Dragon. The IVs reach the battle (gBattleMons: the six IVs are 5-bit
# fields of the word before statStages), the stats don't change.
!new_game()
!give_mon(155, 5)
!warp(0, 11, 0)
expect16 {gPlayerParty+88} 20 hp_20_at_31_ivs_0_evs
!l_menu("STATS")
press DOWN
wait 10
press DOWN
wait 10
press A
wait 120
press A
wait 200
press START
wait 30
# HP IV 31 -> 30
press A
wait 10
press DOWN
wait 10
press A
wait 10
# RIGHT doesn't reach the EVs: this edit is the HP IV again (30 + 10 stops at 31), and B puts the 30 back
press RIGHT
wait 10
press A
wait 10
press RIGHT
wait 10
press B
wait 10
shot 01_editor_minimal_grinding.png
press B
wait 60
expect16 {gPlayerParty+88} 20 stats_unchanged
!battle_trainer(402)
wait 1100
!expect_battler(0, "species", "SPECIES_CYNDAQUIL")
!expect_battler_ivs(0, 0x3FFFFFFE, "ivs_in_battle_hp_30_others_31")
shot 02_battle.png
